action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P11 on GtkBackend on macOS (TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): the two mutually clamped sliders (#82), the wheel inside the forty-row list (#485) and a value change on the compact DatePicker (#473).
# Measured 2026-10-16 from p11-macos-gtk4-final-20261016-012424.png (1520x1296, halved to 760x648; origin=frame, 28 pt native title bar, geometry frame=(580,184) client=(580,212)).
# The AppKit file's Reset/Separate/Collide row and slider drag landed beside their controls on GTK (gtk4-aim-20261016.csv2): the drag at y 276 fell between the sliders (y 250 and 290). The min knob starts at the left end of its track (x 42) because minimum is 0 at launch -- derived from the track, the capture shows it at 50.
# GTK's compact DatePicker has no month stepper: it is a date dropdown (a popover calendar whose month arrows change the day without emitting day-selected) plus hour/minute steppers. The stepper rows therefore use the hour stepper beside it -- up, up, down, net one hour -- the nearest honest equivalent; the month-change path is not exercised here.
# After this file: writes count both sliders after Reset, minimum 50 / maximum 50 and Both at 50, and the hour field one hour after launch with the date unchanged.
# macOS 上 GtkBackend 的 P11:GTK 精簡 DatePicker 沒有月份步進器，改用小時步進器(上、上、下，淨加一小時)。
click,94,331,frame,left,,,Reset counters (was 86;329) -- writes must go to min 0 max 0,macos
sleep,,,,,,600000,,macos
